{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgjabjp1nHyEWwJA6VRDu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bj6K5inHap68zh4KZGWAZT","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"The line opens with a C3 clef and a one-sharp key signature. The first bar has eight staccato 16ths in two groups of four. They rise from B3 and G3 through D4 up to G4 and B4, then fall to G4 and E4. That is bar 80, not bar 79. There is no tied G3 quarter and no G3–A3 16th figure before them. Next comes a C#4 8th (sharp written), an 8th rest and a quarter rest: bar 81. After the barline there is a quarter rest, an 8th rest and a low D3 8th with a slur starting: bar 82. Then Eb3 8th (flat written), 8th rest, 8th rest and a G3 8th: bar 83. Next is a low A3, a high dotted G4–F#4 pair, an F#4 8th and a D4 8th: bar 84. Then an E4 quarter (the copyist writes a natural) and a quarter rest: bar 85. Then a quarter rest, an 8th rest and a D3 8th: bar 86. The line ends with an Eb3 8th, two 8th rests and a G3 8th (slur running off the line): bar 87. So the line holds bars 80 to 87. The end is right, but the line does not include any of bar 79.","right":false,"insights":"The line was easy to match. Its rests and written accidentals (C#, D3, Eb3) pin bars 81–87 clearly, and the staccato 16th arpeggio clearly opens bar 80. The program's mistake was at the start: it probably put the line break one bar early. Checking whether the first bar has bar 79's tied G3 and its 16th figure would have settled it."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5355,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5355},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent